  "rationale": "Every exfiltrate step needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold on the same host, which needs reach_internal and stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin needs admin_dc or admin_adfs. admin_dc needs foothold_dc and stolen_admin. stolen_admin comes only from kerberoast, which needs reach_internal plus a foothold on the appserver or apiserver. That foothold needs stolen_user. One shortest chain is: 1. phish_workstation (gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user). 2. pivot_internal. 3. auth_appserver. 4. kerberoast_dc (gives stolen_admin). 5. auth_dc. 6. escalate_dc. 7. dump_dbadmin_dc. 8. auth_db. 9. escalate_db. 10. exfiltrate_db. Each step is the only way to meet a requirement for the next, and the adfs route has the same length, so no shorter path exists."
